NAC is an apliance or virtual machine that control access to a network, it has complete
visibility into the network profiles and categorizes devices automatically

It evalues and classifies security-policy compliance by user, device, location, operating system, and other criteria
that may detect unusual activity

Many NAC solutions have centralized architecture that improves the control of devices across large and multi-site networks

<-- NAC began as a network authentication and authorization method for devices joining the network wich follows the
IEEE 802.1X standards

The auth method involves 3 parties:
- the client device
- the authenticator
- authentication server

The authenticator could be a network switch or wireless access point that demarks the protected network from the unprotected network

The client provides credentials in the form of a user and passwd, digital certificate or some other means eto the
authenticator, wich fowards these credentials to the server

Depending on the outcome of authentication, the authenticator will either block the device or allow it access to the network

